Date: Mon, 18 Jan 93 10:21:44 PST
From: tcmay@netcom.com (Timothy C. May)
Subject: PHIL: Bilocality and Extropians

Bilocality and Extropians

Pandit Singh has raised issues which I suspect most of us have ignored
because of the way he raised them, e.g., in asserting that ordinary
low-tech yogis in India or elsewhere (Fairfield, Iowa?) can copy
themselves.

Pandit may be right that recent discussions on this list have
resonances with the discussions of bilocality in several cultures.
Some Catholics apparently believe in bilocality (I am told), a point
which I recall Pandit was referring to in the mention of Hans
Moravec's possible Catholic upbringing. And of course there are the
Hindu mythologies/beliefs.

What "bilocality" exists in the Extropian meme complex?

1. Uploading. All the debates about the rights of "copies," sending
copies out to explore the universe, whether a copy is indeed "you,"
and so forth.

2. Quantum bifurcation. Moravec has even speculated, in "Mind
Children," that incredible risks may be taken, because in _some_
universes the risks pay off and in other universes the risks result in
death...but who cares? (I'm simplifying the argument somewhat...)

And shorter term, the prospects for cyberspace suggest the bilocality
issue will hit us very soon: forgery of identities is a kind of
bilocality, agents may be in many places at once, and the whole "True
Names" meme complex suggests bilocalilty as a central theme.

Now this does not mean yogis can make copies of themselves. I still
want to see evidence, as I'm sure James Randi and all the other
skeptics do. And until powerful evidence is presented, I'm atheistic
on the issue (more than agnostic, I'm convinced it isn't possible, by
the many well-studied laws of the universe--but like any rational
atheist, powerful evidence could change my views).

Still, phrased in a philosophical/literary way, Pandit Singh seems
correct in noting the resonances between yogic bilocality, Catholic
bilocality, and the many similar ideas discussed here on this list.


-Tim


